    "work_id": "gez-anaphoras/athanasios",
    "canonical_ref": "EthLit.Athanasios.0044",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Thou Thyself didst know Thine essence and compre- hend Thy Godhead. This bread which is Thy Body we offer to Thee, and this cup which is Thy Blood we pre- sent to Thee for our sin and our transgression, and for the foolishness of Thy people. There is not one of the mysteries of Thy Godhead which Thou didst hide from Thy disciples—(He offereth incense)—Thou didst take ‘bread before them, didst give thanks, bless and break, and give to them saying: Take, eat; this bread is My Body, from which there is no separation.",
